The [[Whetstone]] is a common [[Accessory]] available in the shop for all classes. Buying the [[Smithing for Dummies]] [[Skill]] also grants one [[Whetstone]]. The [[Whetstone]] can give up to two [[Weapon]]s +1 damage, which can be a strong boon in the early game. The Whetstone also acts as a crafting material which upgrades a number of items, mostly [[Weapon]]s. 

Fully upgrading the [[Wooden Sword]] to the [[Hero Longsword]] or [[Burning Blade]] requires a total of three [[Whetstone]]s. Upgrading two [[Wooden Sword]]s to [[Crossblades]] would require four [[Whetstone]]s.

[[Adventurer]]s can combine the [[Whetstone]] with a [[Wooden Buckler]] using a [[Twine]], granting the [[Hero Shield]], which a high quality shield with [[Whetstone]]-like effects (but much stronger).

[[Berserker]]s can catalytically use their [[Utility Pouch]] or [[Forging Hammer]] to improve a [[Whetstone]] into an [[Improved Whetstone]], and then the [[Improved Whetstone]] into an [[Essence of Steel]]. The [[Improved Whetstone]] has more {{icon/star}} slots but is otherwise identical. The [[Essence of Steel]] gives more damage, has even more {{icon/star}} slots, and even buffs {{icon/block}} gain, in addition to being part of some strong crafts.
